1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:07,360
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:13,400
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,660
Woah

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,760
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

5
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,460
nezumiiro no sora no shita

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:31,700
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:37,800
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,980
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

9
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:50,000
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

10
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:56,960
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

11
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:02,540
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

12
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:09,140
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

13
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,900
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

14
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:21,100
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

15
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:28,100
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

16
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:35,820
Hello? Can anyone hear me?

17
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,460
Hello? Anybody?!

18
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,520
Dammit.

19
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:48,040
It's Ling's fault! That idiot prince!

20
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,880
Who do you think you are to call me that?

21
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,000
Huh?

22
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:52,480
Ling!

23
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,520
You can't call the future
emperor of a nation an idiot!

24
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:56,880
Are you alright?

25
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,600
Hold on.

26
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,500
What's wrong?

27
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:05,480
How do I know you're not Envy in disguise?

28
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,040
Oh, come on.

29
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:10,900
Do you want me to recite the hotel
room service menu from top to bottom?

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,740
Alright, you're Ling.

31
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,720
And what about you?
How do I know you're not Envy?

32
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:16,800
You little runt!

33
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,420
Who you calling a little runt? You jerk!

34
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,520
Okay, it's really you.

35
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,740
How did we even get here?

36
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:34,440
Last thing I remember,
Gluttony swallowed us whole.

37
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,660
So you think this cavernous void
is the inside of Gluttony's stomach?

38
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,000
Most likely.

39
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,600
Look, there.

40
00:02:43,780 --> 00:02:46,000
That's the abandoned
house where we were hiding.

41
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:49,000
Also, check this out..

42
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:52,000
And that's the Lieutenant's car!

43
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:55,440
And I'm guessing all the fire
is from the Colonel's attack.

44
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,700
Oh, yeah.

45
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,740
That proves it.

46
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,680
But how could Gluttony's
belly be this huge?

47
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:04,260
I have no idea.

48
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:07,200
But I sincerely doubt that
this is a very pleasant place.

49
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,700
Gimme that.

50
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:09,820
What is it?

51
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,580
[GASP]

52
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:16,380
Ling, look at this!

53
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:18,560
Is that Al's?

54
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,420
Why is it just his hand?

55
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:23,000
Maybe he didn't get swallowed.

56
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,440
Then he's safe.

57
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
He's gotta be freaking out,
wondering where we are now.

58
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:32,480
I wish there was some
way I could contact him.

59
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:37,000
[YODELLING SCREAM]

60
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:40,000
Conveniently awaken, telepathic powers!

61
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,080
Elric brother telepathy!

62
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,640
- Yeah, good luck with that.
- Come in, brother! Come in!

63
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:52,000
This place is like a wasteland
of buildings and human remains.

64
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,160
They're all from different time periods.

65
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,160
I'm starting to wonder if
there's even a way out of here.

66
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:59,340
If not, then I'll make us one.

67
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:00,860
You will, will you?

68
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,180
How and where?

69
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,120
Okay, now drop the torch.

70
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,600
Oh, I get it now.

71
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:09,640
Here goes.

72
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:17,660
[SILENCE]

73
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:20,240
We should have heard it land by now, right?

74
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:22,640
A wall! There has to be a wall!

75
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:24,000
There has to be!

76
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,660
No matter how huge this place is,

77
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:28,300
if we keep heading straight,
we're gonna reach the edge!

78
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,540
There's gotta be some
kind of exit somewhere!

79
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:35,000
I still haven't found her yet.

80
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,300
Where is she?

81
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,500
It isn't like her to just
disappear like this.

82
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,640
Maybe she got eaten by
a stray dog or something.

83
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:45,840
Eaten?!

84
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:50,000
- [WAILING]
- I was joking!

85
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,600
She's not a cat.

86
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:55,640
She's actually a panda, but
she got a disease when she was a baby

87
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,000
and it kept her from growing all the way.

88
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:01,540
I nursed her back to health
after her mother abandoned her.

89
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,340
Since then, she's been
almost like a sister to me.

90
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:09,360
My family, the Chang Clan,

91
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:14,000
is one of the lowest-ranked houses out of
the fifty clans that make up the Xing Empire.

92
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,240
We have little to no power at all.

93
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:18,880
[SOFT GASP]

94
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:21,660
Maybe that's why I was drawn to her.

95
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:26,000
She looked so helpless and weak,
I couldn't help but identify with her.

96
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,660
Hmm.

97
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:32,000
But at the time, I guess I just
took pity on her more than anything.

98
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:35,340
[MEWL]

99
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:39,320
[TINY GROWL]
Ahh!

100
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,820
[SOFT WHIMPERING]

101
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,760
But that changed,
and she became a part of my family.

102
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,300
We've been through so much together.

103
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,300
She's always been with me.

104
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:53,300
It feels so wrong not having her here now.

105
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,580
I don't think I could have
gone through everything I have,

106
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:02,600
without Xiao-Mei by my side.

107
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:06,640
I know for a fact that I couldn't have
made it across the desert without her.

108
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,560
Sure, but that was a
pointless endeavor anyway.

109
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:14,120
Why would you risk your life like that for
something as preposterous as immortality?

110
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:17,000
Because it's the last hope
that my clan has.

111
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,800
If I don't return with a
method for attaining immortality

112
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:23,300
and present it to the Emperor,
it's almost certain my clan will perish!

113
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:29,600
That's...why I risked my life
crossing the desert...with Xiao-Mei.

114
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,000
- [WAILING]
- Come on, cut it out!

115
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
You're gonna drown us all!

116
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,620
Sir?

117
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:47,720
We've got some time
before the sun comes up.

118
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,780
There won't be as many
guards patrolling the streets.

119
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:51,760
Eh?

120
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:55,340
You mean you're gonna help
me try to find her?

121
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,360
He's a good person.

122
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
His people were completely wiped
out during the civil war a few years ago.

123
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:05,520
That's right.

124
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,300
He knows a thing or two about loss.

125
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:12,240
So I'm sure he can identify with
your worries about the fate of your clan.

126
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:15,740
What's the hold up?

127
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:17,140
You coming or not?

128
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,000
Yeah! Let's go!

129
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,660
[GIGGLING]

130
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,600
This is really starting to get old.

131
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,640
Blood doesn't make for good terrain.

132
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,520
I noticed.

133
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:34,680
And we're still not any closer to an exit.

134
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
I'm starving to death.

135
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:44,460
As soon as we're out,
I'll let you order anything from room service.

136
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:49,180
You can eat as much as you
want, and sleep as long as you like.

137
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,380
Ling?

138
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:56,000
I can't make it.

139
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:59,000
Don't tell me...
you're giving up so soon?

140
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:01,000
Are you that pathetic?

141
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:05,000
It's bad enough when you collapse
in the street, but here? Get up!

142
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:06,620
Come on!

143
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,420
Quit being so weak!

144
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,900
Just go.

145
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,200
You spineless jellyfish!

146
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,000
All right, fine then!

147
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,440
Give up and die if you want,
but you're not dragging me down.

148
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,520
I'm seriously leaving you here!

149
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,620
I'm not messing around, Ling!

150
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,340
[GROANING]

151
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,340
I thought you were gonna leave me behind.

152
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:43,000
There's way too many people
I'd be letting down by dying here.

153
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:46,760
And you've got people waiting
for you to get back too, right?

154
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,000
So shut up!

155
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,260
If you're strong enough to—

156
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,380
[YELPS]

157
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,000
So hungry.

158
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:02,000
I wish we could find something to eat.

159
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,440
[PANTING]

160
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:07,000
Well, actually, you know...

161
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:14,920
Leather goods are edible.

162
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,660
We've got a meal.

163
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,420
That should do it.

164
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,380
Here you go.

165
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,240
You don't have athlete's foot, do you?

166
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:29,220
My foot is made of metal, you idiot!

167
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:31,320
Ohh, man.

168
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,380
That shoe filled me up.

169
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,080
I'm sorry, Ed.

170
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,800
And why is that?

171
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
It's all my fault that you're here.

172
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:40,540
It is not.

173
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,560
Besides, this place is a joke compared
to what my teachers put me through.

174
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:47,720
It just sucks that we have
no idea where this place is.

175
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,000
But that's all right.

176
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,600
As long as we've got our health,
we can find an exit outta here.

177
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,400
You're sure optimistic.

178
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,100
Not really. I'm just stubborn.

179
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:02,000
And if I even think about giving up,
I have Al's iron fist to look forward to.

180
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,080
Huh...

181
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,200
What's wrong?

182
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,840
There's something out there.

183
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,280
Is that...?

184
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:15,000
I thought so.
I should've known it'd be you guys.

185
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,680
It's definitely Envy.

186
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,000
- Please show me the way outta here!
- [LING GASPS]

187
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:22,000
You're just going to start begging
the enemy for help like that?

188
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,760
If it means surviving,
I'll be his best friend!

189
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:28,000
- Talk about a sellout!
- It doesn't matter because there is no exit.

190
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,000
[GASPS]

191
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:32,000
You've really gotten us into a fine mess.

192
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
I can't believe you got me
swallowed with you.

193
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,000
You just said swallowed.

194
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,000
So we really are inside Gluttony's stomach?

195
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,740
Well, yes and no.
See, it's a lot more complicated than that.

196
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,160
Just ask the pip—

197
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,820
I mean the alchemist.

198
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:50,080
He should've realized what place this is.

199
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,440
I did notice something
when Gluttony swallowed us.

200
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,000
It was like I had a familiar feeling.

201
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,220
So you do remember then.

202
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,280
This isn't the first time
you've been through this.

203
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,320
[GASP]

204
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:08,780
[GASP]

205
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,200
- Portal of truth!
- [GASP]

206
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,860
But...

207
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:16,340
But it wasn't pitch black
and filled with a sea of blood.

208
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,800
It was more like...
Like an entirely white void.

209
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,760
Oh yeah?

210
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:23,000
So that's what the real one looks like.

211
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,460
The real one?

212
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:29,080
Gluttony is a failed experiment by
our father to create his own portal of truth.

213
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
He's... a what?

214
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,420
Despite how powerful our father is,
he still couldn't create one.

215
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:39,620
We're trapped inside a
defective portal of truth.

216
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:44,540
So this place, it exists somewhere
in between reality and truth.

217
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,200
In between?

218
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,480
And I can assure you that
there's no way out of here.

219
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:53,840
The only option we've got is to
sit here until our strength runs out.

220
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,460
And that's it.

221
00:11:56,320 --> 00:12:00,280
All we can do is wait here to die.

222
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,440
Fullmetal Alchemist.

223
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:06,520
Fullmetal Alchemist.

224
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:13,240
No way... Don't think I'm
falling for any of that crap!

225
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:15,300
I know you're lying to us, Envy!

226
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:17,340
You're lying, aren't you?!

227
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:20,100
So there really isn't a way out?

228
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:22,700
We're gonna die here?

229
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:26,920
Wait... No... Hold on...

230
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,000
I can't die here...

231
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:32,040
What's Al gonna do if I die?

232
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:37,320
We made a promise, and he...
He needs me to get back to normal.

233
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Dammit!

234
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:42,280
I wanna know who your father is!

235
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:44,780
Who would try to create their own portal?!

236
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,840
It's Führer Bradley, isn't it?!

237
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,000
[SCOFFs]

238
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:50,000
What, are you serious?

239
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:54,220
Huh, nice try, but King Bradley's
nothing more than a Homunculus.

240
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:55,000
[GASP]

241
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:56,620
Told you so.

242
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,220
The Fifth Laboratory...

243
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:04,000
Human lives sacrificed to make Philosopher's Stones...

244
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,360
Homunculi...

245
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:12,400
And if the Führer's on your side,
then I'm guessing you're the ones behind Ishval.

246
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:14,000
Oh, Ishval!

247
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:18,740
[CACKLING] I couldn't have asked for a
more enjoyable job than that.

248
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:21,900
You remember the incident
that started the war, right?

249
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:23,000
[GASP]

250
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:28,120
I had always heard it was because a military
officer accidentally shot an Ishvalan child.

251
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,000
Yep.

252
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:34,000
And the one that proudly pulled
the trigger was none other than yours truly.

253
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,660
[GASP]

254
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,160
Excuse me.

255
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,000
I know what happened in Ishval.

256
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,120
Yoki told me.

257
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:11,180
You have no idea how good that felt.

258
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:15,000
I ravaged their entire
country with a single bullet.

259
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,780
[LAUGHS]
I mean, talk about invigorating!

260
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:20,740
Oh, and the best part?

261
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:23,160
The officer that I pretended to be?

262
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:28,560
He was actually a moderate who would always
publicly oppose the military's occupation in Ishval.

263
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,000
And listen to this?

264
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:36,400
The poor fool couldn't come up with a plausible
defense and they court-martialled him!

265
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:41,160
You know, I don't think I'll ever get over
how easily manipulated humans are.

266
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:43,000
[CACKLING]

267
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
So you're responsible.

268
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,780
You were the one who shot
and killed that poor innocent child.

269
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:52,000
You destroyed my hometown.

270
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,260
You drove out the Ishvalans.

271
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:58,000
You're the one who turned
Scar into a murderer.

272
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:00,000
And it was you.

273
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:03,000
You're the reason
Winry's parents were killed!

274
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,000
You're the one to blame!

275
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,180
What the hell?

276
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,680
He didn't budge.

277
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,120
Okay, then. If that's how you want it.

278
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:18,000
Ed, get back!

279
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:26,260
I'm gonna show you two boys
something neat before we die.

280
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:30,000
Consider it a parting gift!

281
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,480
Did you notice his footprints back
when we were all fighting in the forest?

282
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,920
What? No.

283
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,060
What's your point?

284
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:42,340
Just that he's freakishly
heavy for the size of his body.

285
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,300
He might be a bit bigger than he looks.

286
00:15:59,000 --> 00:15:59,760
Damn!

287
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,220
What the hell?

288
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,700
How is that a Homunculus?!

289
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,780
They're supposed to be artificial humans, right?

290
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:11,960
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

291
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:33,580
What should... What do I do?

292
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,120
I have no idea.

293
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,440
Hmm...

294
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:40,980
What do I do?

295
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:42,660
I'm scared.

296
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:45,240
I don't want Father to be mad at me.

297
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:46,380
Huh...

298
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:48,380
What did you say?

299
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:50,360
You have a father?

300
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,620
Uh-huh.

301
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,720
Is he the one that made the Homunculi?

302
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,780
Father made us.

303
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,900
[GASP]

304
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,520
Where does everything he swallows go?

305
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,780
It's gotta be some kind of trick.

306
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,860
Come on, think!

307
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:12,060
We made a promise and
Brother might still be alive!

308
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:15,000
I can't just give up now!

309
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:16,980
Gluttony...

310
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Will you take me with you?

311
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,540
Will you take me to meet your father?

312
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:24,860
I guess so.

313
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,000
[GASP]

314
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:29,200
He'll be happy since
you're a human sacrifice.

315
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:30,000
Uh—

316
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:32,000
Oh, sure, right!

317
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,500
That's why he'll wanna meet me!

318
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:38,000
And I guess I'll find out...
what that means.

319
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,580
In regards to the search
for potential sacrifices,

320
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,380
our only candidates
are the Elric brothers.

321
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:47,580
What about Dr. Marcoh?

322
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:48,820
Isn't he ready?

323
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,480
We still have Kimblee.

324
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:54,640
I doubt that Kimblee could muster up
the nerve it takes to open the portal.

325
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:56,460
That reminds me.

326
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:00,500
How have things been progressing
along with Mustang's candidacy?

327
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,640
That's a question for the Fuhrer.

328
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,780
He plans on having a
nice long talk with him.

329
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:12,340
Tell me, why are you
bothering to let me live?

330
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:16,060
Because you aren't going to learn
your lesson if you're dead, soldier.

331
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,580
And the military?

332
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,000
How long has all this been going on?

333
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:26,000
The Homunculi have been controlling
this entire nation since its inception.

334
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:30,740
So all this time you've been sitting
back and laughing at our struggles?

335
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,120
I saw you at General Hughes' funeral.

336
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:36,000
Your hands were trembling.

337
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:38,620
So did you fake that as well?

338
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:44,560
Why must everyone make such a
fuss over the death of a single soldier?

339
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:50,480
The moment a soldier dons his uniform,
he accepts the reality that he might be buried in it.

340
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,100
And about my hands,

341
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:58,460
Hughes' child screeched throughout
the entirety of his funeral.

342
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:03,000
My hands were trembling with anger.

343
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
How can you even say such a thing?

344
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,000
You have a child too.

345
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,200
You're speaking of Selim?

346
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:12,520
He's more well behaved than that.

347
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:19,000
And how do you think he'd react if he
found out that his father was a Homunculus?

348
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,880
Was that a threat?

349
00:19:22,380 --> 00:19:24,000
You'll have to do better.

350
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:28,820
Selim will never work as a
point of weakness in my life.

351
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:32,060
But you on the other hand...

352
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:35,880
I know exactly who to use as your weak point.

353
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:41,280
Lieutenant Hawkeye!

354
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:43,080
What's wrong, Sergeant?

355
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,680
I received a memo from
the Personnel Bureau.

356
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:50,980
And, well, I'm being transferred
to the Southern Command Center.

357
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,000
They transferred you?!

358
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,580
And I'm not the only one.

359
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,360
Breda's being sent to the Western Command.

360
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:02,000
And Warrant Officer Falman's been
reassigned to the Northern Command.

361
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,120
[GASP]

362
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,120
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

363
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,120
Lieutenant Hawkeye?

364
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,020
Yes, sir.

365
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,560
I'm Yakovlev from Personnel.

366
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:19,520
Am I being transferred?

367
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,000
And my name is Storche.

368
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,180
I'm the personal assistant to Fuhrer Bradley.

369
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,240
I need you to take this.

370
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:28,260
Am I being reassigned, sir?

371
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,520
That's correct.

372
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:33,160
I'd like to look at them.

373
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,000
What is this?!

374
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:42,220
This can't be right!
Are you sure that these are my orders?

375
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:43,860
Where are they sending you?

376
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:49,800
First Lieutenant Riza Hawkeye is to
report for duty at Central Command Center...

377
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,000
[RELIEVED EXHALE]

378
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,920
As personal assistant to Fuhrer Bradley.

379
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,000
[GASPS]

380
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:57,000
It's as simple as that.

381
00:20:57,320 --> 00:21:00,000
She'll be under my watch from now on.

382
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:06,360
[DISTORTED VOICES]

383
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:09,160
Play with me! Let's play!

384
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:13,000
Hell no! You go and play by yourself!

385
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,600
Uh...this isn't good!

386
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,600
[DISTORTED LAUGHTER]

387
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:19,800
Ah!

388
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,200
Ling!

389
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:26,120
[DISTORTED CACKLE]

390
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,340
Ed!

391
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,760
Can you make a weapon?

392
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,000
You got it!

393
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:38,080
With this ocean of blood,
there's plenty of iron to work with!

394
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:46,000
You have the tackiest sense of taste.

395
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:49,580
Aw, come on!
I think it looks pretty damn sharp, myself!

396
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,280
[DISTORTED LAUGHTER]

397
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,000
Can we take him?

398
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,120
I doubt it. He is a giant monster.

399
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:02,000
And then on top of that,
I'm pretty sure he broke two of my ribs.

400
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,160
Yeah, I'm pretty beat up myself.

401
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:06,320
But that's beside the point.

402
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:09,640
All that matters now is
filling him with some pain!

403
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:18,400
Are you sure this is
the right way, Gluttony?

404
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:19,400
Uh-huh!

405
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:23,560
But this is the way...it can't be....

406
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:27,520
Your father is living in Central?

407
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,320
Let it all out, let it all out

408
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

409
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

410
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

411
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,680
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

412
00:22:56,680 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

413
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

414
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

415
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:23,480
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

416
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:31,540
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

417
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,820
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

418
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

419
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

420
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

421
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

422
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:05,280
The lost souls of the forgotten past litter
the path leading toward the unknown future.

423
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:07,560
The young man knows he must fight...

424
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:12,820
But the only way for him to discover the truth
is to fully explore the darkness that engulfs it.

425
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:16,680
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

426
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:20,440
Episode 26: Reunion

427
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:26,880
I refuse to say goodbye when I'm certain
that our paths will cross once again in the future.
